00:00:03.409 --> 00:00:09.309
Attack on titan, in Japanese, the attack titan,
is literally about Eren, attacking all of

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:16.650
Humanity as a titan. In the end, Eren becomes
what he hates most. It's an anti-war story,

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:22.260
about a protagonist that turns out to have
been the villain, but also victim of the story

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:32.890
all along. And Eren is probably the most misunderstood
character I have ever seen.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:39.620
So attack on titan is finally over, the reviews
are in, aaaand - everyone seems to have hated

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.870
it. I have come across are broad spectrum
of things people didn't like about how the

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:49.270
story wrapped up, but the most-commonly named
factor I heard, was without any doubt Eren,

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:54.520
the supposed main character of the story,
massacring his way through the last few arcs,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:59.781
without giving us the big twist at the end
that everyone was apparently hoping for. No

00:00:59.781 --> 00:01:06.520
satisfying ending, no coherent character development,
no big aha-moment to reveal that Eren was

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:12.881
the good guy all along, that we all wanted
him to be. And admittedly, I personally have

00:01:12.881 --> 00:01:17.410
not been a fan of some of the writing throughout
the series, with the Manaka explicitly stating

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:23.050
his difficulties with writing and even understanding
his own main character.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:27.860
And yet, I want to argue with this video,
that Eren's character was consistent from

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:33.810
start to finish and that his ending not only
makes sense, but is actually just as deep

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:38.590
as you were hoping for. But make sure to let
me know your perspective, once you've watched

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:48.200
it.

