00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:53.691
In many ways, I think that Eren, and more
generally attack on titan as a whole, fell

00:02:53.691 --> 00:02:59.130
pray to its own success. It was the story
that popularized anime and manga outside of

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:04.580
Japan as probably no other story before, even
more than big shots like Dragon-ball, One

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:12.550
Piece and Naruto, pushing the genre into the
mainstream. And so, many people, me included,

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:17.830
put Attack on Titan side by side with many
other Shounen and other mainstream stories

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:23.420
as a more dark and bloody version of them.
And some kept that up until the very end,

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:28.430
until the very last chapter. However, when
the larger world and narrative behind the

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:34.180
story was reveled, with Marley and Eldia and
all the political, social and moral implications

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:39.060
around them, maybe later than necessary, I
understood that Attack on Titan does not only

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:45.160
not belong into the shounen genre, but in
many ways uses the anime and manga format,

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:56.870
to depict an incredibly dark and depressing
story. So it makes total sense to me that

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:10.180
its creator, Hajime Isayama, was taken aback
by its international success.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:15.090
While we all knew that Eren Jaeger was no
conventional shounen Hero, Isayama never saw

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:21.430
him as any sort of hero for the story in the
first place. He is the protagonist, sure,

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:25.990
but as it turned out after the time skip,
we were watching the story of the complex

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:31.400
and morally grey villain of the story. The
backstory and ultimately the downfall of the

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:37.460
man who killed not only a character here or
there, or even a crowd of bystanders, but

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:43.430
80% of the worlds population. Can we please
appreciate for a second how bizarre that wiki

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:44.780
entry is?

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:51.380
So yes, my opinion is that Eren is both morally
grey and capable of good, but looking at the

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:56.650
end-result nonetheless the villain of the
story. He is however, a villain that tries

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:11.590
to be the hero, though he ultimately fails.
He is a beautiful example of the rare negative

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:16.500
character arc. Negative not because the arc
is bad, but in the sense that the character

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:22.600
develops, but instead of growing to become
a better person, he grows to become a worse

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.930
one. Let me explain:

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:29.730
Normally, a positive arc, we know from most
of our heroes, has the hero start from a negative

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:36.160
place. He has some ideal or believe that has
a negative impact on him and those around

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:42.340
him, so he needs to change. Throughout the
story, he might have moments of darkness and

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:47.790
failure, but generally moves in the right
direction until in the end, when the moment

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:52.930
of truth comes, he finally understands his
flaw and makes the right choice, becoming

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:58.620
a better person and giving us the happy end
we need. A negative arc, such as Eren's is

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:03.460
the inversion of this. The character starts
with a similar flaw, but from a much more

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:08.610
positive looking start point. Eren always
has his angry and violent side and difficulties

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:15.380
being vulnerable, but his hard work and determination
to protect his friends and fight for freedom,

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:20.020
seem to point him in the right direction.
However instead of moving into the right direction,

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:25.340
we see Eren slowly falling deeper and deeper
into his feelings of rage and helplessness,

00:06:25.340 --> 00:06:31.790
punctured by moments of positivity, for instance
during his fight with Annie, after Armin sacrificed

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:43.400
himself for his sake or during the events
in the crystal cave. But despite these moments

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:49.139
of insight, Eren degreases further and further
away from his original goal, until finally

00:06:49.139 --> 00:06:58.300
he is faced with the choice to murder 80%
of humanity or simply stop. And he chooses

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:06.150
the rumbling over his humanity. In many ways,
he has the most linear development out of

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.520
all characters in the last part of the story.
Because most character arcs in Attack on Titan

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:11.740
actually seem to be somewhat circular. Annie
still wants to run away back to her father,

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:15.419
because that’s what he told her to do when
he was a little girl. Mikasa starts with the

00:07:15.419 --> 00:07:21.759
desire to be a normal family with Eren, and
after all she went through, she is still codependent

00:07:21.759 --> 00:07:35.550
on him until the end. Armin still sees himself
as weak and unimportant, despite wielding

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:41.990
the strongest titan and being a commander.
It's a story about kids turned into soldiers,

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:47.300
that can't grow up and move on from their
childhood ideals and beliefs, due to all the

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:52.039
cruelty and violence around them, something
Falco and Gabi represent in the latest arc,

00:07:52.039 --> 00:08:05.240
by mirroring Eren and 
co. These characters don't follow a character

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:10.850
arc. As much as they follow a character circle,
breaking out of their bad habits and beliefs,

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:13.550
only to fall right back into them.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:17.580
And even though you may or may not like it,
and believe me, I totally get it, I prefer

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:25.850
happy ends myself, but this has nothing to
do with bad writing. It's just unconventional.

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:28.960
So how did it all come to this?

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.229
One of my favorite things about Attack on
Titan's writing, was the shamelessly abrupt

00:08:33.229 --> 00:08:38.659
change of narrative perspective from before
to after the time skip. For the first three

00:08:38.659 --> 00:08:43.729
seasons, until we reach the sea, we basically
share the same misleading and propagandized

00:08:43.729 --> 00:08:50.199
perspective of our protagonists. The premise
seems pretty clear: All that is left of humanity

00:08:50.199 --> 00:08:55.470
lives inside the walls of the last standing
bastion, facing the inhuman and soul-less

00:08:55.470 --> 00:09:01.640
titans, that with their grotesque looks and
moments, hunt humans. Attack on titan seemed

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:17.040
ah pretty clear set up to me for humanity
vs the monsters. Oh oh, okay, so now Eren

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:22.220
can transform into a titan, but it's okay
he only uses this power to fight the evil

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:26.069
monsters. Argh, but then we find out, that
he's actually not the only one that can do

00:09:26.069 --> 00:09:31.740
this, actually it turns out all the titans
were actually not soul-less beasts to begin

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:46.339
with, but people turned beast against their
will. So it's actually Attack on Human's I

00:09:46.339 --> 00:09:49.040
guess? And that actually fits pretty perfectly.
Uff and there is a lot of intrigue and political

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:54.309
games going on, and the ones in power chose
to leave thousands of their soldiers and civilians

00:09:54.309 --> 00:10:00.149
to be slaughtered by the titans, before letting
anyone learn the truth. Slowly but steadily,

00:10:00.149 --> 00:10:05.709
season by season, the horror of the titans
makes way to the horror of people and season

00:10:05.709 --> 00:10:14.769
3 ends with World War II imagery, leaving
the titan powers a mere weapon of mass destruction.

00:10:14.769 --> 00:10:19.319
With the time skip, just as Eren and co, we
suddenly break free from the worldview, which's

00:10:19.319 --> 00:10:24.600
propaganda has been spoon-fed to us since
chapter 1. As it turns out, what we thought

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:30.660
to be the vast last resort of humanity, was
actually just a tiny island in a world rich

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:35.199
with people and cultures. And as it turns
out, Attack on titan is not a story about

00:10:35.199 --> 00:10:43.139
humans fighting monsters, it's a story about
humans fighting humans or monsters fighting

00:10:43.139 --> 00:10:49.249
monsters. A story about racism and war and
how they lead to a never-ending cycle of hatred

00:10:49.249 --> 00:10:54.750
and oppression. The titans in the end only
exists as a tool of oppression and the cause

00:10:54.750 --> 00:11:00.000
of racism in this world, which is ultimately
why their true origin and the secret behind

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.079
their creation doesn't matter in the end.

00:11:05.079 --> 00:11:14.019
The main catalyst for Eren's inability to
grow is the lost of his mother. Having her

00:11:14.019 --> 00:11:19.989
unconditional love taken away, traumatizes
him so extremely that it makes him incapable

00:11:19.989 --> 00:11:26.119
of growing into a true adult. However, we
know that Eren already carried anger and violence

00:11:26.119 --> 00:11:32.009
inside him, when he murdered the two traffickers,
who try to take Mikasa. Both we and Mikasa

00:11:32.009 --> 00:11:37.040
took it as a pure act of kindness however,
however the version of Eren that gently wraps

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:42.110
the scarf around her head, the version that
Mikasa believes him to be until the very end,

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:49.379
and that undoubtedly exists inside Eren, never
makes it past his anger. And this is the key

00:11:49.379 --> 00:11:55.119
to Eren's last words at the end, that left
so many people disappointed. The truth however

00:11:55.119 --> 00:12:01.489
is, that Eren, never had a clear motivation
for his actions. Yes he wanted to protect

00:12:01.489 --> 00:12:10.699
his friends and change the world, but above
all, Eren always hated the fact that 

00:12:10.699 --> 00:12:20.739
the world was cruel and he had no agency in
it. Eren wanted the choice to do something.

00:12:20.739 --> 00:12:25.259
He was so traumatized by not being able to
do anything about his mother being killed,

00:12:25.259 --> 00:12:31.480
that he took control over the world, to stop
the world controlling him. Instead of facing

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:38.749
and accepting his own humanity and vulnerability,
he selfishly tries to control everything around

00:12:38.749 --> 00:12:43.709
him. If you read closely in the last chapter,
Eren changes his reasoning from “I was doing

00:12:43.709 --> 00:12:48.449
it all to set up you as heroes of the world”
to&nbsp;“I would have done it anyway even if

00:12:48.449 --> 00:12:55.369
you didn’t come to stop me” to&nbsp;“I don’t
know. I just wanted to.” Eren makes up stories

00:12:55.369 --> 00:13:00.480
and reasons for his atrocities, looking for
a way to give them a greater meaning, when

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:06.299
there really is not. That's why it only makes
sense, that there was no great twist in his

00:13:06.299 --> 00:13:11.519
plan at the end. Eren felt justified in his
actions at every step of the way. If eren

00:13:11.519 --> 00:13:15.740
really wanted to do it for his friends, why
did he hurt them, as armin said. What is the

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:18.040
point? But it's all about having a choice
for Eren. And to get that choice, that ultimate

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:30.480
freedom he wants, he takes it away from everyone
around him. So the fact that Eren's reasoning

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:36.559
doesn'T make scenes, is actually not a flaw,
but a fundamental part of his personality.

00:13:36.559 --> 00:13:41.649
Eren begins his life with&nbsp;“You were born
into this world, you’re free to live however

00:13:41.649 --> 00:13:48.480
you want” and ends his life wishing he was
never born, and that’s the ultimate tragedy

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:53.790
of his character arc. Not that it was inevitable
he would eventually do these things, but because

00:13:53.790 --> 00:14:00.429
it was not and Eren chose to do them anyway
instead of choosing literally anything else.

00:14:00.429 --> 00:14:04.959
As we know there were plenty of options for
him to just stop and everyone begging him

00:14:04.959 --> 00:14:09.959
to do so. Therefore, despite claiming Mikasa
and Armin as the reason behind all of his

00:14:09.959 --> 00:14:16.019
actions, they weren’t, because he was incapable
of making the simple choice to be with them

00:14:16.019 --> 00:14:26.720
and grow up with them which is all they ever
wanted from him. All Eren ever wanted was

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:32.360
agency and control, but what he really needed
was allowing himself to be vulnerable and

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:39.069
accept the unconditional love he had from
Armin and Mikasa, that his foil Zeke was denied

00:14:39.069 --> 00:14:47.069
all his life.

00:14:47.069 --> 00:14:52.850
What unites the tragic sties of Eren, Zeke,
Reiner and many others, is that they all act

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:59.149
based on a sense of entitlement because of
what has happened to them. They were oppressed

00:14:59.149 --> 00:15:04.470
and the victim of a brutal life, and they
used that fact as justification for their

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:10.230
actions even past the point where they had
gained so much power, that they became the

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:23.759
oppressors. All of them committing genocide
and war crimes, still feeling like they are

00:15:23.759 --> 00:15:26.379
the true victims here.

00:15:26.379 --> 00:15:30.940
Eren gets the lesson, that he is not the only
one that suffers in this world shoved in his

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:37.160
face over and over again. But right until
the end, he fails to see the true feelings

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:42.999
of the people around him, because he won't
even allow himself to face his own fears,

00:15:42.999 --> 00:15:47.910
hopes and dreams. He rejects Armin's dreams,
even though they used to be his own, just

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:58.040
as he rejects Mikasa's love, even though he
clearly loves her.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:03.339
There is definitely room to criticize the
writing in Attack on Titan, a brutal anti-war

00:16:03.339 --> 00:16:07.759
story about monster adults creating monster
children in a world where the motivations

00:16:07.759 --> 00:16:18.319
and beliefs of every single character come
from their traumatizing childhoods. However,

00:16:18.319 --> 00:16:24.579
I think you can't deny the beauty in Eren
literally becoming the Attack titan that threatens

00:16:24.579 --> 00:16:30.600
to wipe out all of humanity, exactly what
the story seemed to be about at the start.

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:36.009
The essence of what he used to hate the most,
a giant monster, that toys with the lives

00:16:36.009 --> 00:16:49.809
or all for no good reason whatsoever. Eren
becoming the enemy of humanity then is the

00:16:49.809 --> 00:16:55.119
tragic story of a traumatized kid, robbed
of his chance for a happy and normal life

00:16:55.119 --> 00:16:57.620
by the cruel world around him.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:04.600
The unseeing, but bright happy end of Eren's
gruesome arc then, is that his dream of getting

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:10.850
rid of the titans, the symbol for oppression
and death, ends with his death. And Mikasa,

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:17.870
who was unable to break free from her codependent
love for him, is the tragic hero who takes

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:22.920
the life of the man she loves, still seeing
in him the beauty of the world, that Eren

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:23.830
never could.

